From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:43:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 50/52] hw/usb/hcd-imx21: Cancel the packets in flight before a
 restore

Packets in flight are not migrated; after a restore their ETDs run
again. A restore into a running machine (loadvm) left them in flight,
though: their ETDs were skipped as busy, and a late completion would
write into the restored ETD and data memory. They are now cancelled
before the load.

Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Fc77Z6fVVe4rWJxPT
---
 hw/usb/hcd-imx21.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/usb/hcd-imx21.c b/hw/usb/hcd-imx21.c
index 2a3e61a1d..92f93a247 100644
--- a/hw/usb/hcd-imx21.c
+++ b/hw/usb/hcd-imx21.c
@@ -905,6 +905,21 @@ static int imx21_usbotg_pre_save(void *opaque)
     return 0;
 }
 
+static int imx21_usbotg_pre_load(void *opaque)
+{
+    IMX21USBOTGState *s = opaque;
+    int i;
+
+    /*
+     * A restore into a running machine: its packets in flight belong to
+     * the state being replaced, and must not complete into the new one.
+     */
+    for (i = 0; i < NUM_ETD; i++) {
+        imx21_usb_cancel(s, i);
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
 static int imx21_usbotg_post_load(void *opaque, int version_id)
 {
     IMX21USBOTGState *s = opaque;
@@ -931,6 +946,7 @@ static const VMStateDescription vmstate_imx21_usbotg = {
     .version_id = 2,
     .minimum_version_id = 2,
     .pre_save = imx21_usbotg_pre_save,
+    .pre_load = imx21_usbotg_pre_load,
     .post_load = imx21_usbotg_post_load,
     .fields = (const VMStateField[]) {
         VMSTATE_UINT32_ARRAY(regs, IMX21USBOTGState, USBOTG_REGS),
